# exoplanets
# It is no longer necessary to manually download exoplanets from the internet, as the data are now retrieved automatically.
# However, when the manual download was required, this is how it was done:
# https://exoplanetarchive.ipac.caltech.edu/cgi-bin/TblView/nph-tblView?app=ExoTbls&config=PSCompPars
# open the above link in a browser, manually select to include the columns:
# HD ID, Inclination, Epoch of Periastron, Argument of Periastron, True Obliquity, RA[deg], Dec[deg], Distance[pc], V Magnitude.
# and click Update.
# Then click the download (save icon) button, choose CSV format, and click the green Download Table arrow.
# Save the resulting file in the alienorum/catalogs/ folder.

